# Principal source notes for P2/P3

These are source-only implementation constraints, not dynamic evidence. No new source execution or fake artifact is authorized by this note.

- `RoleRequestV5` has no campaign/round field. `FeedbackRoundInputV5` has actual campaign/index/owner. Runtime constructs the corresponding primary RoleCallKeyV5 in `_complete_role` only after request factory returns; the request is persisted just before invocation. Factory guard must consume actual inputs. Ledger guard must use `load_unique_role_request_entry_by_sha256` to recover the exact persisted call; do not infer its round from role memory.
- `_load_verified_role_ledger_v5` already authenticates exact persisted requests, every prospective old bound, sequence/prior cumulative totals, responses/terminals and recorded usage without constructing a live ledger. `_authenticate_role_invocations_v5` binds complete journal packages to this ledger and requires identical counts/order. Its inputs must cover all real prior packages, including earlier roles of the currently active round; no fake current package and no current reservation exists yet at admission.
- The factory guard runs before current request persistence. The ledger guard runs after current request persistence but before reservation. A request census may allow exactly that one authenticated actual persisted current call in the ledger path; it must not accept arbitrary orphan requests. On normal partial recovery previously completed roles may be rebuilt by the factory; the native helper must distinguish authentic replay/continuation from a fresh attempt without charging another three-role reserve.
- H1/H2 completed resource readers can authenticate individually settled prior rounds. H1 requires a real event journal and authenticates original round configs/owners through saved identities; no need to invoke it for a truly fresh current investigator before its intent exists. Existing readonly workspace/mount history constructors are approved; no operational executor/gateway/ledger construction.
- `_authenticate_completed_history_census_v5` is deliberately whole-campaign and excludes pending/current unsupported requests/resources. Do not call it on a partial campaign or create a filtered repository wrapper to force it to pass. Reuse narrowly appropriate helpers, and keep completed-history full census in P4 authoritative.
- `LocalArchiveReducerFactoryV5.verify_projection(..., repair=False)` authenticates actual checkpoint/archive and scheduling/critic dependencies. Count evaluated distinct round indices exactly as summary: committed records with status evaluated and campaign_evidence present, intersected with actual successful cleanup round indices. A terminal without an evaluated committed record is not an evaluated round. Existing failure/novelty authorities retain precedence.
- Historical per-round journals, cleanup and checkpoint evidence lack cross-round publication timestamps. The admitted round's reconstructed prior-round prefix and ordered actual receipt cumulative amounts prove logical eligibility. Stored campaign/round epochs can prove only their own deadline relation. Do not claim global cleanup/config/checkpoint publication ordering.
- Existing `recover_typed_state_index(namespace, key, expected_value)` authenticates exact preexisting value and sole missing index before publishing that index. P1 immutable readers never call it. P3 may call only after explicit expected policy, original identities and real no-start/no-spend freshness have independently authorized the crash recovery. No replacement values and no implicit recovery by discovering an orphan.

These notes refine implementation mechanics without expanding canonical schemas, capabilities or the accepted sidecar design.
